## Before any work

1. Confirm repo path, remote, and branch `main`.
2. Run `git fetch origin` and `git status -sb`.
3. Verify push works: `git push origin main` (or dry-run). If push fails, stop and apply the single fix below before coding.

## Every update

1. Make the requested change (minimal diff).
2. Test locally: `node --check js/app.js` and `python3 -m http.server 8091` in repo root.
3. Commit on `main` with a clear message.
4. `git push origin main`
5. Confirm Pages reflects the change (fetch live URL or check Actions deploy).

## Push failure — one fix

Load your GitHub SSH key and use SSH remote (key must be added to your GitHub account):

```bash
ssh-add --apple-use-keychain ~/.ssh/id_ed25519
cd ~/Documents/GitHub/Analyzer-Schedule-Generator
git remote set-url origin git@github.com:Jasonburke2888/Analyzer-Schedule-Generator.git
git push origin main
```

Do not ask the user to run git commands unless push still fails after this.
